{"records":[{"id":"835fcfbvhs","title":"Preparation of CRISPR/Cas9 and gRNA plasmids","description":"Human genome engineering has been transformed by the introduction of the CRISPR (clustered regularly interspaced short palindromic repeats)/Cas (CRISPR-associated) system found in most bacteria and archaea. Type II CRISPR/Cas systems have been engineered to induce RNA-guided genome editing in human cells, where small RNAs function together with Cas9 nucleases for sequence-specific cleavage of target sequences. Here we describe the protocol for Cas9-mediated human genome engineering, including construct building and transfection methods necessary for delivering Cas9 and guide RNA (gRNA) into human-induced pluripotent stem cells (hiPSCs) and HEK293 cells. Following genome editing, we also describe methods to assess genome editing effi- ciency using next-generation sequencing and isolate monoclonal hiPSCs with the desired modifications for downstream applications. Keywords: genome engineering • CRISPR • human stem cells","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2016-12-12T12:58:15.307Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/835fcfbvhs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/835fcfbvhs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"George","last_name":"Church","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Experimental Method"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"65pfcj4j4m","title":"Protocol of CRISPR-Cas9 knockout screens for identifying ferroptosis regulators","description":"Ferroptosis, an iron-dependent programmed cell death triggered by excessive lipid peroxidation, has shown promising therapeutic potentials in human diseases. Here, we describe a protocol of a CRISPR-Cas9 loss-of-function screen to identify regulators in response to different inducers of ferroptosis. We emphasize the steps of library amplification, drug treatment, high-throughput sequencing preparation, and bioinformatics analysis using Model-based Analysis of Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 Knockout (MAGeCK). We also present a method to discover the regulators of ferroptosis and verify the potential targets efficiently.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-10-24T01:46:48.793Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/65pfcj4j4m","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/65pfcj4j4m"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Yang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wei","last_name":"Gu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR/Cas9","Ferroptosis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"s3jtdhjdbs","title":"Supplementary data for Michaelis et al., 'Protein import motor complex reacts to mitochondrial misfolding by reducing protein import and activating mitophagy'","description":"Supplementary data for Michaelis et al., 'Mitochondrial import loss induces mitophagy without membrane depolarization'. We hypothesized that inhibition of mitochondrial protein import induced mitophagy independent of mitochondrial depolarization. This dataset contains raw Illumina sequencing data for all samples from a genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 screen for mitophagy regulators. The genome-wide library is Brunello from Doench et al Nat Biotechnol. 2016. We found that the pre-sequence translocase-associated motor complex PAM controls mitophagy induction. Loss of PAM caused a loss in protein import and was sufficient to induce mitophagy without depolarization.\nThe samples have been sequenced on an Illumina NextSeq 500 in single end mode with 75+8 cycles. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-08-05T15:38:53.752Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/s3jtdhjdbs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/s3jtdhjdbs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jonas","last_name":"Michaelis","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Melinda","last_name":"Brunstein","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Süleyman","last_name":"Bozkurt","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ludovico","last_name":"Alves","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Martin","last_name":"Wegner","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Manuel","last_name":"Kaulich","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Christian","last_name":"Pohl","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Christian","last_name":"Münch","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Proteomics","Mitochondrion","Mitophagy","Genetic Screening","Next Generation Sequencing","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"npwwxbvcnc","title":"Systematic Review GBM + Immunotherapy + TMZ","description":"A collection of clinical trials involving the use of temozolomide and an immunotherapy on patients with glioblastoma. These files show the papers that were gathered in the initial collection as well as the final set of papers from the screening process. The data shows that 10 papers were ultimately selected from 444 papers. These papers were listed as controlled, double-blinded, clinical trials using temozolomide and an immunotherapy on patients with glioblastoma. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-07-27T03:37:28.49Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/npwwxbvcnc","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/npwwxbvcnc"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Brendan ","last_name":"Chen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Janet","last_name":"Alder","orcid":"0000-0002-5694-4946"}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cancer","Temozolomide","Immunotherapy","Astrocytoma","Glioblastoma Multiforme"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"33tm3dd9dw","title":"FAME-CRISPR: Improved CRISPR-Cas9 Genome Editing via HDAC Inhibition and Engineered Virus-Like Particle Delivery ","description":"Raw data deposited for \"FAME-CRISPR: Improved CRISPR-Cas9 Genome Editing via HDAC Inhibition and Engineered Virus-Like Particle Delivery\" by Djamshidi et al-Cell Reports Methods","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-09-25T15:53:30.358Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/33tm3dd9dw","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/33tm3dd9dw"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mahbod","last_name":"Djamshidi","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Sanger Sequencing","Immunofluorescence"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"vtvxykv2cr","title":"2020_Cell reports resubmission tables","description":"All tables associated with our paper titled \"High throughput CRISPR screening identifies genes involved in macrophage viability and inflammatory pathways\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-12-15T08:44:50.23Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vtvxykv2cr","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vtvxykv2cr"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Susan","last_name":"Carpenter","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Macrophage","Immunity","Innate Immunity","Screening","Pooled Analysis","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"xvk2gk4hw3","title":"Data of Murine Trophoblast Organoids as a Model for Trophoblast Development and CRISPR/Cas9 Screening","description":"Raw data for figures in Murine Trophoblast Organoids as a Model for Trophoblast Development and CRISPR/Cas9 Screening","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-10-25T15:27:04.321Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xvk2gk4hw3","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xvk2gk4hw3"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Qian","last_name":"Mao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Developmental Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3ctpx4k6jp","title":"Porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus upregulates SMPDL3B to promote viral replication by modulating lipid metabolism","description":"We generated a collection of porcine genome-scale CRISPR/Cas9 knockout (PigGeCKO) cells on a PAM background.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-26T18:53:54.241Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3ctpx4k6jp","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3ctpx4k6jp"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"huanh","last_name":"Shen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Agricultural Biotechnology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3frm3mnkpc","title":"Supplemental material for MAPKs/AP-1, not NF-κB, is responsible for MCP-1 production in TNF-α-activated adipocytes","description":"This study, for the first time, reveals that MAPKs/AP-1 but not NF-κB signaling is responsible for MCP-1 production in TNF-α-activated adipocytes. All of raw data are provided below, classified by each result (figure) in the manuscript.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-06-01T17:39:53.872Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3frm3mnkpc","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3frm3mnkpc"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"小雨","last_name":"张","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Adipocyte","Physiopathology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"pv8t3hbg4t","title":"Proteasome-Bound UCH37 Debranched Ubiquitin Chains to Promote Degradation. Deol et al. ","description":"The following documents show sequencing data confirming CRISPR/Cas9 genome editing of cell lines, all gels used for analysis, and mass spectrometric chromatograms and LC traces. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-10-09T23:09:46.22Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/pv8t3hbg4t","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/pv8t3hbg4t"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Eric","last_name":"Strieter","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kirandeep","last_name":"Deol","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sean","last_name":"Crowe","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jiale","last_name":"Du","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Heather ","last_name":"Bisbee","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Robert","last_name":"Guenette","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Mass Spectrometry","Gel","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":129520,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":101,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":129520,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":128892,"restricted":64,"embargoed":564},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2185},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":667},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":461},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":409},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":398},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":394},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":376},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":321},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":263},{"id":"https://ror.org/00k4n6c32","name":"European Commission","count":218}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":126898},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1904},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":181},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":131},{"id":"df228bbb-ac66-410f-8c66-f61608d63d95","name":"University of South Florida","count":78},{"id":"2a9d1b7d-e447-466f-888f-aa6f84e575e4","name":"